<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23174" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-fervĕfăcĭo</span></b> ,
			fēci, factum, 3, v. a. (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>pass.</i>
			fīo, factus, fĭēri), <i>to cause to boil in</i> any thing; or simply <i>to cause to boil</i>, <i>to boil</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infervefacito paulisper,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 156, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">liquatum acetum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					12, 17, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum infervefiunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 271</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnia infervefacta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					9, 13, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
